** Looping Statements **

	1. While -> used when number of iterations are not fixed or not known
			 -> it is called as entry control loop becuase it checks the condition at the beginning of the while loop
			 -> syntax: //initialization
			 			while(condition)
			 			{
			 				//code
			 				increment/decrement;
			 			}

	2. Do-While -> used when loop should execute at least one time
				-> it is called as the exit control loop because it checks the condition at the end
				-> even if the condition is false do-while performs the statement inside block atleast once
				-> Syntax: do
							{
								//code
								increment/decrement;
							}while(condition);
							
	3. for Loop -> used when number of iterations are known
				-> syntax: for(initialization ; condition ; increment/decrement)
							{
								//code
							}
							

** Array **

	-> Array is collection of similar datatypes 
	-> Contiguous Memory Allocation, allocates single block of memory.
	-> Syntax: a. Declaration1: data_type array_name[] = {...};						// Decides on number of elements.
				  Declaration2: data_type array_name[] = new data_type[size]; 		//Fixed Size	
	-> uses indexing : position of array elements is called as array 
	
	Advantages:
		-> Can store homogeneous datatypes
		-> Easy for accessing, searching elements because of indexing.
		-> Easy to modify, updation.
		
	
	Disadvantages:
		-> Can't Store Heterogeneous Datatypes
		-> Fixed in Size.
		-> slow for insertion and deletion.
		
	Types of Arrays:
		-> 1. Single Dimensional Array - represents in single square brackets
		-> 2. Two Dimensional Array    - represents using 2 square brackets : [] []
		-> 3. Multi-Dimensional Array
				  
